==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*unnaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|unnan}}, {{cog|goh|unnan}}, {{cog|dum|onnen}} ({{cog|nl|gunnen}}), {{cog|non|unna}} ({{cog|sv|unna}}, {{cog|da|unde}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ang|/ˈun.nɑn/}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb}}

# to [[grant]] or [[bestow]] (+ ''dat'' (person) + ''gen'' (thing))
# to [[wish]]
# to [[intercede]]

====Conjugation====
{{ang-conj|unnan<pp>}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ang|geunnan}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|enm|unne}}
** {{desc|en|own}} {{q|to acknowledge, concede}}, {{l|en|own up}}

